    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d605">

                <pb facs="0533" n="521" xml:id="pg521"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.6363 St 2/505</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President of the Standard Oil Company of New
                        Jersey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Farish</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New
                                York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1940-12-16"
                            >December 16, 1940</date>.<lb/>[Received December 17.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Welles</hi>: Thank you very much for your
                    letter of December 13 on the Bolivian matter. I had already written the enclosed
                    letter to Mr. Bonsal, so I am enclosing a copy to bring you up to date.</p>
                <p>I do hope you can go forward with the negotiations as suggested.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. S. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Farish</hi></signed></closer>



